# `/mago.bat` is deliberately NOT listed here. It is a tracked artifact, shipped
# by the alignment task list and present in the repository template, because
# Infection cannot run Mago on Windows without it. See issue 59.

# Spec Kit is used locally for planning but its scaffolding is not tracked in
# this repository: `.specify/` and `specs/` are working notes that complete their
# purpose when alignment lands. `.github/skills/` is tracked, because the skills
# there describe this package to agents.
#
# Installed presets live under `.specify/presets/` and are ignored with it. To
# track a preset, remove `/.specify/` below; `.specify/presets/.registry` is then
# the authoritative record of what is installed, and without it the preset
# directory is ignored and every template falls back to core.
#
# Ignored instead are the artifacts that belong to the machine rather than the
# project.
/.specify/
/specs/
/.specify/extensions/.cache/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Benchmark corpus (generated, do not commit)
/test/benchmark/corpus/*
!/test/benchmark/corpus/.gitkeep
